{
  "id": "repressilator-six-state-biology",
  "name": "Repressilator with explicit mRNA and protein stages",
  "description": "Six dimensionless states retain transcription/translation stages; this is not the distinct two-gene toggle switch already in the library. Reconstructs a retired flowless concept. Dimensionless Box1 form; alpha216, alpha0=0.216,beta5,n2 are illustrative choices in the customary repressilator regime, explicitly not claimed to reproduce a particular experimental figure. Asymmetric initial protein [0,0,1] and horizon80 chosen to excite and inspect cyclic response. Signed net-rate flows encode equations, not material transfer claims. No clamps or hidden state resets. Adaptive Radau resolves the initial rapid mRNA/protein transient; a coarse fixed RK4 step failed independent-reference accuracy screening.",
  "source": "https://doi.org/10.1038/35002125",
  "reference": "Elowitz and Leibler (2000), A synthetic oscillatory network of transcriptional regulators, Nature403:335-338, Box1.",
